# Agent root entry (CLAUDE.md — Claude Code)

This is the Claude Code root entry. It **imports** the always-on rules (Claude Code expands `@path`)
and signposts everything else; it holds no rule bodies itself. `AGENTS.md` (for Codex) reaches the
same rules by **inlining** them, since Codex has no `@import` — the two files are **runtime-equivalent,
not byte-identical**. Both are rendered by `scripts/render-agent-entries` from
`platform-internals/templates/` (framework-owned) plus `team-context/agent-entry.team.md` (team-owned):
edit those, never this file.

When working on a mounted business repo, first read its `team-context/mounted-repos/<id>.md` (id = the repo's id
in `workspace.local.yaml` `repositories[]` — the gitignored sidecar that holds the local mount list;
see `agent-instructions/mount-points.md` for why `workspace.yaml`'s own `repositories:` key stays a
frozen `[]` placeholder).

